   $q$How do the passage's ideas about practical need and public resistance interact?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Resistance came only from the railway company, which wanted to protect its own timetables from change.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"Practical need and resistance never met, because the residents did not learn about railway time for decades.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"Public resistance was so strong that the railway company finally returned every station to local sun time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Residents objected at first, but as newspapers, schools and the post office came to depend on trains, practical need won out.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Residents objected at first, but as newspapers, schools and the post office came to depend on trains, practical need won out.$q$, $q$Paragraph 4 describes objections and then says "Gradually, though," institutions adopted railway time because their business depended on the trains. Nothing in the text says the company ever went back to local time.$q$, 'draft', 'a0f9180e-714c-52c6-9e4d-582f063048ad')
