   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Letting the sea back into Calder Bay restored a marsh that protects the shore and supports wildlife, offering a model for other coasts.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Every coastal town should tear down its seawalls at once and allow the ocean to flood its low fields.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Fishing crews at Calder Bay persuaded the parks office to cut gaps in the wall so they could catch more fish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The earthen wall at Calder Bay was built by hand generations ago so that farmers could graze cattle on the land.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Letting the sea back into Calder Bay restored a marsh that protects the shore and supports wildlife, offering a model for other coasts.$q$, $q$The passage explains the decision, the shoreline and wildlife benefits, and the project's value as a model. The final paragraph limits the claim to "the right places," so the "every coastal town" choice overstates it.$q$, 'draft', 'cf6ed342-15bb-50cf-9eb3-94e012db2791')
