   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Old varnish can yellow and hide a painting's colors. Conservators remove it slowly with carefully chosen solvents, make their own additions removable after past damage, and decide case by case how far to clean.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Early restorers were reckless and destroyed many great works of art. Today's conservators are far wiser, and museums should trust them completely to decide how every painting ought to look.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"At the Ostrava Art Hall, a restorer in the 1920s cleaned a landscape too aggressively. He removed thin glazes of color, and the painting has looked flat ever since.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Varnish protects paintings from damage, so conservators add a fresh coat every few years. They choose bright varnish that makes old colors look newer than they were.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Old varnish can yellow and hide a painting's colors. Conservators remove it slowly with carefully chosen solvents, make their own additions removable after past damage, and decide case by case how far to clean.$q$, $q$The first choice covers the problem, the method, the principle and the open question without judgment. The Ostrava choice is accurate but summarizes only one example from paragraph 4.$q$, 'draft', '5b9a9e3e-ad90-5eb8-8cbb-7f6932e21313')
