  ('98ddf453-67b2-5b19-9379-2252753af5c0', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-main-idea-summary'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How do the opening paragraph and the final sentence work together to shape the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The opening introduces the safety objection, and the ending proves that the objection was correct all along.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The opening describes a lost sky, and the ending presents the standard as a way to recover it, framing the practical reasons with a shared sense of loss.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The opening states that the sky itself has changed, and the ending admits that lighting cannot restore what has been lost.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The opening and ending focus on cost, which shows that saving money is the writer's only real concern.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-emphasis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The opening describes a lost sky, and the ending presents the standard as a way to recover it, framing the practical reasons with a shared sense of loss.$q$, $q$The first paragraph ends "The sky has not changed. Our lighting has," and the last sentence promises "a sky our grandparents would recognize," so the two frame the money and wildlife reasons. The second choice contradicts the opening's statement that the sky has not changed.$q$, 'draft', '0f82031e-88f1-5a7f-a969-d3e6f4fc3e6a')
