   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The Brackenridge library held deeds, council minutes, newspaper clippings and the payroll books of the old mill.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The students' oral history project showed that people's memories add to a town's history, if they are gathered and checked with care.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Written records are unreliable, so towns should base their histories only on the memories of older residents.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Former mill workers in Brackenridge used hand signals because the machines were too loud for them to hear.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The students' oral history project showed that people's memories add to a town's history, if they are gathered and checked with care.$q$, $q$The final paragraph states both parts of the idea: history lives "in its people," and gathering it "responsibly takes patience, preparation and a habit of checking." The students checked interviews against written records, so the third choice contradicts the text.$q$, 'draft', 'abc639b4-7adb-5242-af70-ee4acc8917c8')
