  ('4b42a218-c0fa-5362-b038-9afcd0268ddb', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-main-idea-summary'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Former mill workers described the roar of the machines, their hand signals and lunch hours by the river. One woman told how families pooled money to help a flooded neighbor.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Brackenridge's students did remarkable and inspiring work that every town should copy. Their recordings are far more meaningful than the dull deeds and council minutes in the library.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Brackenridge's library had many documents but few personal voices, so students recorded forty residents. The interviews added details missing from records, and the students compared accounts because memories can change.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Brackenridge's library had many documents but few personal voices, so students recorded forty residents. Their interviews finally revealed the true story of the town that the official records had hidden.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"distorts-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Brackenridge's library had many documents but few personal voices, so students recorded forty residents. The interviews added details missing from records, and the students compared accounts because memories can change.$q$, $q$The first choice covers the gap, the project, what it added and the careful checking without judgment. The second choice begins the same way but claims the interviews revealed "the true story," which ignores paragraph 4, where students declined to choose one version as the truth.$q$, 'draft', 'abc639b4-7adb-5242-af70-ee4acc8917c8')
